+++ b/old-origin/README.md
@@ -0,0 +1,16 @@
+# Legacy origin files
+
+Deploy these to the **old** origin (`https://dailygrind.example.com`) to hand the
+installed app over to `https://app.dailygrind.example.com`.
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `.well-known/web-app-origin-association` | Authorizes the new origin to take over the installation. Serve as `application/json`. |
+| `manifest.webmanifest` | Old manifest with a `migrate_to` hint so installed users are prompted without visiting the new site. |
+| `migrate-bridge.html` | Lets the new origin read the user's saved settings (localStorage) once. Must be frameable by the new origin (no `X-Frame-Options: DENY`). |
+| `migration-banner.js` | Banner for browsers without origin migration support. Add `<script src="/migration-banner.js" defer></script>` to the old pages. |
+| `icon.svg` | App icon referenced by the manifest. |
+
+Both origins must be same-site (share the registrable domain); migration across
+different domains is rejected. If you change either origin, update every file
+here plus `manifest.webmanifest` and `migrate-settings.js` at the repo root.
